{
 "_about": "What stands where in the fantasy world's places (rules: core/fantasy_layout.gd; sizes: data/fantasy/props.json). kinds: one list of rules per place kind (data/fantasy/world.json places.kind). A rule is ONE thing {model, at} or SEVERAL {models, count, ring} or a WALL {wall, gate, gates, ring, tower}: the wall closes right up to its gates, the road through each gate is kept clear, tower = a model built into the wall beside each gate. at and ring are fractions of the place's flat radius (at_m and ring_m = metres); face: in | out | any; even = spaced evenly around the ring; station = a crafting station stands there; $ in a model name = the region's building scheme; extras = that many things from the region's own list below. sites: small spots scattered through the country (metres), region_sites: how often each kind turns up in a region. Things never overlap: a thing that does not fit is left out. walk_over: the models nobody bumps into (they lie flat, hang overhead or are too small); everything else in the world is solid to players and creatures. station on a SEVERAL rule = each one placed is that station (it gets 60 tries to fit instead of 5; polish1 E5: the coach house of walled towns); no_salt: true on a rule added later keeps the chance placements of the rules after it where they were. (polish1 item 123) the textless signposts in the place rings are gone: game/fantasy_places.gd puts named road signs where each road leaves a place. (polish1 E4) a place may name its own rules with world.json 'layout' (the Harvest King's arena: arena_threshing, a threshing ground of stooks, flail racks, haystacks and loose straw round the old threshing floor). (polish1 F1b) crossing_<kind> (road, ford, pass, ferry, voyage): a country's crossings, planned facing OUT of the country (-z out, +x to its right; core/fantasy_layout.gd _facing turns them); the pier of a ferry or ship landing and a ford's stepping stones are added by code (_crossing_extras). (polish1 F3) manor, village_fishing, village_orchard, village_wood, hamlet, hamlet_coast, hamlet_mill, lodge: the plans of Amberfield's own places (data/fantasy/places/amberfield.json \"layout\").",
